<title>USA: Smith Barney lists 15 &quot;exceptional names&quot;.</title>
<headline>Smith Barney lists 15 &quot;exceptional names&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney on Tuesday released a list of 15 stocks selected as &quot;Exceptional Names,&quot; a portfolio it views as &quot;particularly attractive&quot; over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>Last year's group rose 39.6 percent in the year to June 30, 1997, versus a 32 percent rise for the S&amp;P 500, Smith Barney said.</p>
<p>Among the stocks on this year's list are Avon Products Inc, BellSouth Corp, Cisco Systems Inc, Dresser Industries Inc, Duke Energy Corp and First Bank System Inc.  </p>
<p>Also on the list were Eli Lilly and Co, Mirage Resorts Inc, Monsanto Co, Motorola Inc, Philip Morris Cos Inc, Textron Inc, and Wal-Mart Stores Inc.  </p>
<p>Warner-Lambert Co and Williams Cos Inc rounded out the list.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1721))</p>
